{"type":"message","id":"2f3d1279","parentId":"2faeb2ff","timestamp":"2026-05-12T17:23:44.939Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Karen's right — I got ahead of myself on tiered routing. OpenClaw's fallback chain is **failure-only**, not task-based. My bad.\n\nSo the real options are simpler:\n\n**Option A — `llama3.1:8b` primary, cloud fallback** ✅\n- One model per session\n- 6-10s response time\n- If it fails/errors, bumps to kimi k2p5 automatically\n- What Karen already configured\n\n**Option B — Manual switching** ✅\n- `/model ollama/llama3.1:8b` when you want local\n- `/model kimi-coding/k2p5` when you want speed\n- Full control, more typing\n\n**Option C — Keep cloud primary for now** ✅\n- What you're actually experiencing right now"}],"timestamp":1778605592328}}
